{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"Authored the P1 intent spine set. No new IDs or status changes; P3 trace cells remain intentionally untouched.\n\nAmendments:\n\n- SR-208\n  - `requirement`: replaced the off-spine loop-writer rule with the held snapshotted-registry lane-claim rule and marked-autonomous-commit arm. Why: state-based protection covers all lane deliveries.\n  - `rationale`: replaced. Why: explains why author identity cannot govern the hold.\n  - `acceptance_criteria`: replaced. Why: defines claims, exception, lane/squash walk, exclusions, and fail-closed reads.\n\n- LLR-246\n  - `detail`: replaced. Why: specifies the claim predicate, bound-CLARITY exception, lane rider, retired slot rung, and narrowed marked arm.\n  - Explicit retirement rewrite: “`integrate._merge_refusal runs it again ... over the whole range of every loop lane`” → “`The slot's loop-lane held-status rung does not run.`”\n  - Explicit marker narrowing rewrite: marker coverage of all loop writers/lane commits → “`Under the loop marker, a commit outside a claimed lane ... is refused ...; a marked commit inside a lane is judged at landing.`”\n\n- LLR-249\n  - `detail`: “`acceptance_record.committed_status_moves`” → “`held_status.committed_status_moves`”. Why: records the planned P3 module move.\n\n- LLR-278\n  - `detail`: removed the held act-ledger CLARITY sentence and added the binding-identity condition: “`A held CLARITY re-attestation is actable only when ... digest equal ...; an absent, malformed or unequal identity refuses it ... before launch.`”\n  - `test_refs`: appended P5–P7 digest, binding, and pre-launch refusal tests. Why: binds the new identity behavior.\n  - Explicit retirement rewrite: “`... held_reattest_refusal ... [verdict/CLARITY checks]`” → removal of that ledger arm; identity binding now governs held CLARITY re-attestation.\n\n- TC-241\n  - `method`, `expected`, `evidence`: replaced. Why: verifies the lane/state predicate, squash behavior, exclusions, malformed carriers, and narrowed marked arm using the planned held-status suites.\n\n- TC-278\n  - `method`, `expected`, `evidence`: replaced. Why: verifies digest production/preservation and held-CLARITY identity refusal at both act and landing.\n\n- IF-129\n  - `data`: added `approved_text_digest`.\n  - `notes`: new. Why: defines approved-cell classification and carrier/empty-cell invariance.\n\n- IF-196\n  - `rationale`, `requestors`, `data`, `notes`: amended. Why: describes the shared held-claim/rider/marked-refusal surface without moving its owner prematurely.\n\n- IF-220\n  - `notes`: appended that `verdict` is audit-only and no held-rung rule requires the ledger cell. Why: records the retired dependency.\n\n- IF-287\n  - `rationale`, `data`, `notes`: amended. Why: defines optional binding identities, reader/writer behavior, and malformed-cell handling.\n\n- IF-296\n  - `rationale`, `data`, `notes`: amended. Why: makes unequal/missing held identity a pre-launch, row-naming refusal.\n\nArms map:\n\n| Requirement arm | TC clause | Planned test(s) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Approval-status/copy/retirement claim | TC-241 method | `test_a_live_flip_into_approval_is_a_claim`, `test_a_copy_entry_move_or_retirement_is_a_claim` |\n| Non-claims | TC-241 method | `test_not_judged` |\n| Held tier universe | TC-241 method | `test_HELD_TIERS_equals_the_snapshotted_tiers`, `test_an_unmapped_registry_is_held` |\n| Lane rider and squash walk | TC-241 method | `test_the_rule_rides_the_lane_commit_walk`, squash tests |\n| Lane held-SN/refusal coverage | TC-241 method | `test_a_lane_approving_a_held_SN_with_its_copy_is_refused`, coordinator/reclaimed-lane tests |\n| Trunk refresh and malformed carrier | TC-241 method | `test_a_refresh_merge_carrying_trunks_approvals_lands`, unreadable/unparseable cases |\n| Narrowed marker arm | TC-241 method | marked/unmarked trunk, loop-writer, and marked-lane tests |\n| Digest shape and carrier invariance | TC-278 method | three `test_the_digest_*` tests |\n| Binding identity grammar/persistence | TC-278 method | binding round-trip, malformed-cell, brief/bind/outcome tests |\n| Held CLARITY exact-text exception | TC-278 method | exact-text, changed-text, missing-identity, MEANING+BLESS, and pre-launch act tests |\n\nGap: no test is assigned to the P3 symbol relocation itself because the required traced cells remain bound to current carriers until P3; the plan’s characterization and bootstrap tests cover that move.\n\nChecks run:\n\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict`: emitted existing advisory warnings; its long run did not return a final exit summary before the tool timeout.\n- `trace.py --strict`: completed with `orphans=0 integrity=0 interface-findings=0`; existing advisories only.\n- Required empty-list pytest invocation: started, but a retry failed with `WinError 5` while cleaning the mandated `review-tmp/wi-851-terra` directory because workers from the earlier full invocation still held it. No test result is claimed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nNothing else is unsettled in the authored rows; the outstanding verification limitation is the locked pytest base-temp directory."}}
